WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 11.6 · Fundraising, Revenue & Sustainable Business Models
Foundations and philanthropic grants

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Shortlist foundations on evidence of fit, not on how much they have.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Check priorities, geography, eligibility and whether they fund core costs.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Use the contact route each foundation prefers.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Record every decision and learn from rejections.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Riverside Repair Hub (Hybrid · charity with a trading company, United Kingdom)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Riverside: community fund 5/5 (bid by December); Local Trust C 4/5; a national retailer’s scheme dropped: national charities only.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You create a scored shortlist of foundations.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
